s:106552:"{
"lastpushid": 320,
"pushes": {"14": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 42e1acb39affae65d50ced864d28672d67aa0181 with FIREFOX_91_0esr_BUILD2 a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a1d9a6c9e7af68c5be409e343e972b4376e0e641", "parents": ["42e1acb39affae65d50ced864d28672d67aa0181"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628118737, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "15": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121854", "files": ["services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "941deecae1ecaeef524c8c9c2c6b5c8dc75d93de", "parents": ["a1d9a6c9e7af68c5be409e343e972b4376e0e641"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628176403, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "16": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717717 - Remove a jit-test that's very slow in the C++ interpreter. r=jonco, a=test-only\n\nThe C++ interpreter has code to run the pre-barrier verifier at every opcode. This\ncan make testing without JITs really slow and should probably be fixed at some point.\nFor now remove this particular test because these tests tend to be brittle anyway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121505", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug1717405.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2e0f54e46f5fad967d327b8b8aabb37702acf175", "parents": ["941deecae1ecaeef524c8c9c2c6b5c8dc75d93de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722239 - Move Linux telemetry tests to WebRender. r=jmaher, a=RyanVM\n\nautoland\n\n--- target_task_set@d201b02824ec\n+++ target_task_set@ao_ci_telemetry\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n\nmozilla-central\n\n--- target_task_set@d201b02824ec\n+++ target_task_set@ao_ci_telemetry\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-ccov-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-ccov/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-telemetry-tests-client-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-shippable/opt-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-telemetry-tests-client-e10s\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120803", "files": ["taskcluster/ci/test/test-sets.yml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a836000d1a1744b4d2868533d94ad31f6d5cd9cb", "parents": ["2e0f54e46f5fad967d327b8b8aabb37702acf175"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721945 - Move Linux mochitest-browser-chrome tests to Software WebRender. r=jmaher, a=RyanVM\n\nautoland\n\n--- target_task_set@27882dfe84fb\n+++ target_task_set@ao_ci_linux_browser_chrome_swr\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-a11y-checks-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/opt-mochitest-devtools-chrome-a11y-checks-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-a11y-checks-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n\nmozilla-central\n\n--- target_task_set@27882dfe84fb\n+++ target_task_set@ao_ci_linux_browser_chrome_swr\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-ccov-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-ccov/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-qr/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-a11y-checks-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-fis-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-mochitest-devtools-chrome-a11y-checks-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-shippable/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-a11y-checks-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-shippable/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-shippable/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-fis-e10s\n\nmozilla-release\n\n--- target_task_set@27882dfe84fb\n+++ target_task_set@ao_ci_linux_browser_chrome_swr\n+test-linux1804-64-asan-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-asan/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n+test-linux1804-64-shippable-qr/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-swr-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64-shippable/opt-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n-test-linux1804-64/debug-mochitest-browser-chrome-e10s\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120977", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_startup_syncIPC.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.ini", "taskcluster/ci/config.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/mochitest.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/test-sets.yml", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/tests.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "46647da49d40a2f8b1a792104c1b8de421b0aece", "parents": ["a836000d1a1744b4d2868533d94ad31f6d5cd9cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722721 - Suppress new TSAN failures for WebRender. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121090", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "24036e5c754f1ea244aa000b80e4476ccb96ce2e", "parents": ["46647da49d40a2f8b1a792104c1b8de421b0aece"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel Maher \u003cjmaher@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722726 - Move Linux tsan tests to WebRender. r+a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121791", "files": ["dom/base/crashtests/crashtests.list", "editor/libeditor/crashtests/crashtests.list", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/svg/reftest.list", "mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp", "taskcluster/ci/test/mochitest.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/reftest.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/test-platforms.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/web-platform.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/xpcshell.yml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/moving-between-documents/before-prepare-iframe-parse-error-external-module.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/moving-between-documents/before-prepare-iframe-success-external-classic.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2bb5adcb5e6c07644deafb93a80cac7fcf437bb5", "parents": ["24036e5c754f1ea244aa000b80e4476ccb96ce2e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel Maher \u003cjmaher@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722913 - Port remaining tests on Linux to WebRender. r+a=RyanVM\n\nrebased to esr91 version of patch from https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1722913, https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121212\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121792", "files": ["dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.ini", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.ini", "taskcluster/ci/test/marionette.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/mochitest.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/reftest.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/test-platforms.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/test-sets.yml", "taskcluster/ci/test/xpcshell.yml", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/tests.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.rst", "tools/tryselect/test/test_fuzzy.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3ca5f0ecdaaf88b39f0e7d969e4a235edd0f9ceb", "parents": ["2bb5adcb5e6c07644deafb93a80cac7fcf437bb5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628196527, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "17": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update, r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122091", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "820004fa5e68dc6da164d9ffb5149fd901960c3f", "parents": ["3ca5f0ecdaaf88b39f0e7d969e4a235edd0f9ceb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628512428, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "jcristau@mozilla.com"}, "18": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Update configs. IGNORE BROKEN CHANGESETS CLOSED TREE NO BUG a=release ba=release", "files": ["browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6b0dbbc667c520e3c702c2206157e66e27d880f5", "parents": ["820004fa5e68dc6da164d9ffb5149fd901960c3f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628525863, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld-merge"}, "19": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mozilla Releng Treescript \u003crelease+treescript@mozilla.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 42e1acb39affae65d50ced864d28672d67aa0181 with FIREFOX_91_0esr_RELEASE a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "93cf735dc12fdfc885900ed90c87d03c7417ae75", "parents": ["6b0dbbc667c520e3c702c2206157e66e27d880f5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628599694, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "ffxbld"}, "20": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jeff Gilbert \u003cjgilbert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717078 - Enable av1 pref for color_quads tests. r=gfx-reviewers,jrmuizel a=test-only DONTBUILD\n\nOtherwise, outside of Nightly, av1 will be disabled on Android, and\nthese tests will be both orange and not useful.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122302", "files": ["dom/media/test/reftest/color_quads/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f0d01ca6f02d1ea12d4d443d1175bec4d5b34267", "parents": ["93cf735dc12fdfc885900ed90c87d03c7417ae75"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628700785, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "21": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrei Oprea \u003candrei.br92@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724966 - Fix newtab test setup to be independent of timezones. r=Mardak, a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122286", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/test/unit/asrouter/ASRouterTargeting.test.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8516cac68b08c1ab673722a79c17a28f7036329e", "parents": ["f0d01ca6f02d1ea12d4d443d1175bec4d5b34267"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1716307 - Only run test_SocketScalars when there's a socket process. r=janerik, a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122012", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_SocketScalars.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/xpcshell.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "70e15013adc7202efb5de7b8d7a791c739c747ec", "parents": ["8516cac68b08c1ab673722a79c17a28f7036329e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719173 - Update metadata, r=whimboo a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122066", "files": ["testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webdriver/new_session/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5625f6202672f341fc6e9a3bae801365511fa234", "parents": ["70e15013adc7202efb5de7b8d7a791c739c747ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709945 - Adjust color_quads reftest limits to pass on local machine. r=jgilbert, a=RyanVM\n\nThese limits allow these tests to give expected results on my local machine.\nThese results should not be impacted by gecko changes against this bug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119547", "files": ["dom/media/test/reftest/color_quads/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d25ca98c2528eb75bf76823f9615e7cc2c19e70e", "parents": ["5625f6202672f341fc6e9a3bae801365511fa234"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709945 - Change full range h264 test so it expects full range to work on windows. r=jgilbert, a=RyanvM\n\n720p.png.bt709.bt709.pc.yuv420p.h264.mp4 should match the AV1 case on Windows\nonce bug 1709945 fixes our handling. Adjust the test to reflect this.\n\nWe allow for a small margin of error in the test, as try machines record small\ndifferences when running the test. At time of writing, 7 pixels differ by 1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119548", "files": ["dom/media/test/reftest/color_quads/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "230a249c8f7f903643dbc2057d251f8604a1edce", "parents": ["d25ca98c2528eb75bf76823f9615e7cc2c19e70e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709945 - Correctly record changes in VideoInfo found during MediaChangeMonitor::Create. r=alwu, a=RyanVM\n\nDuring MediaChangeMonitor::Create we create a CodecChangeMonitor and parse it an\ninitial config. Following this the CodecChangeMonitor may already have detected\nchanges.\n\nPrior to this patch, if the CodecChangeMonitor detected any changes, we did no\npick up on those. This meant that things such as full range h264 video were not\nbeing correctly identified.\n\nThis patch ensures that we update the config we pass to take into account the\nVideoInfo from the CodecChangeMonitor.\n\nDepends on D119548\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119549", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wrappers/MediaChangeMonitor.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "244b85f8afd41e54ec3942c8edba835670403569", "parents": ["230a249c8f7f903643dbc2057d251f8604a1edce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1709945 - Relax short.mp4 reftest swgl fuzzy-if pending investigation. r=jgilbert, a=RyanVM\n\nRelax these tests so we can land the bug without having a perma fail. Bug\n1720346 has been raised to investigate the issue further.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119790", "files": ["dom/media/test/reftest/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3cf0b0f6948a263c98b721ca315ca03ee98f633", "parents": ["244b85f8afd41e54ec3942c8edba835670403569"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Lemley \u003crob@thunderbird.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1670147 - Set values for AccessibleHandler.dll CLSID/IIDs at configure time. r=Jamie,glandium a=RyanVM\n\nAllow for downstream projects such as Thunderbird to set different GUIDs for\nAccessibleHandler to avoid clashes when both applications are installed.\nThe GUIDs themselves can be defined in confvars.sh or in branding/configure.sh\ndepending on the specific needs of the application. Fallback GUIDs are in\nold-configure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D118124", "files": ["accessible/ipc/win/handler/HandlerData.idl", "accessible/ipc/win/handler/HandlerDataUUID.h.in", "accessible/ipc/win/handler/moz.build", "browser/branding/aurora/configure.sh", "browser/branding/nightly/configure.sh", "browser/branding/official/configure.sh", "browser/branding/unofficial/configure.sh", "browser/installer/windows/moz.build", "browser/installer/windows/nsis/defines.nsi.in", "old-configure.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "958aef401f3c27231c426fc6e00024b0741470a6", "parents": ["e3cf0b0f6948a263c98b721ca315ca03ee98f633"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gian-Carlo Pascutto \u003cgcp@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721326 - Allow dynamic PTHREAD_STACK_MIN. r=glandium, a=RyanVM\n\nhttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120708\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120972", "files": ["js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSContext.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7f9b9624c400dc847dc0053ebe35fbe63353a3d2", "parents": ["958aef401f3c27231c426fc6e00024b0741470a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721326 - Use small stack for DoClone(). r=jld, a=RyanVM\n\nPatch author is Florian Weimer \u003cfweimer 'at' redhat.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120709", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/launch/SandboxLaunch.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "600365d8b24068e8105773830270cf86478aa487", "parents": ["7f9b9624c400dc847dc0053ebe35fbe63353a3d2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628705430, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "22": {"changesets": [{"author": "Bryce Seager van Dyk \u003cbvandyk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1582575 - Shutdown MediaCache::sThread before nulling it. r=alwu, a=RyanVM\n\nsThread is used in assertions of functions running on sThread. Prior to this\npatch, we would null sThread before shutting it down, this meant sThread could\nbe null while resolving any tasks remaining on that thread. This could lead to\nnull derefs.\n\nThis patch changes the ordering of shutdown so that sThread is not nulled until\nafter shutdown has taken place.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119333", "files": ["dom/media/MediaCache.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b3cad12e9c6ba6d7242426233f13c0193c18090c", "parents": ["600365d8b24068e8105773830270cf86478aa487"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1716028 - Update crossbeam-deque. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121550", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-deque/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-deque/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-deque/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-deque/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b8bab1920c25beff5ffb73489782982f720cf6a7", "parents": ["b3cad12e9c6ba6d7242426233f13c0193c18090c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1716622 - Limit ImageData typed array to 2 GB. r=edgar, a=RyanVM\n\nAfter we enabled support for large ArrayBuffers on 64-bit platforms, we could\nalso create larger ImageData objects. WebIDL bindings check for large ArrayBuffer{View}s\nbut not when they're wrapped in an ImageData.\n\nIt seems safest to limit ImageData arrays to the old 2 GB for now until we need larger\nbuffers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121595", "files": ["dom/bindings/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/bindings/test/test_large_imageData.html", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d27e0d4d4c34a509844dabb4c892f778a741748f", "parents": ["b8bab1920c25beff5ffb73489782982f720cf6a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1672640 part 1: Flatten logic and update comments in FlexItem::ResolvedAscent(). r=TYLin, a=RyanVM\n\nThis patch doesn't affect behavior; it just refactors some logic to have an\nearly-return and reduce indentation, to make the next patch in this series\neasier/simpler.\n\nWhile we're at it, this patch also updates & extends some neighboring\ncode-comments to be more specific & more correct about how this code behaves\nand its limitations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121921", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "efba45b1f9169312afdbdc92c457bcca7e27aee0", "parents": ["d27e0d4d4c34a509844dabb4c892f778a741748f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1672640 part 2: Fall back to GetNaturalBaselineBOffset to ask flex items what their baseline is. r=TYLin, a=RyanVM\n\nOur earlier call to nsLayoutUtils::GetFirstLineBaseline/GetLastLineBaseline\nworks in most cases, but those APIs don't handle every frame type and fails for\ntext control frames (for example).  This new call should handle those cases\nby directly asking the frame for its baseline.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121922", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/flexbox-baseline-nested-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/flexbox-baseline-nested-001.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c4b852a855cf50a991b30c22405c4ed0f891badf", "parents": ["efba45b1f9169312afdbdc92c457bcca7e27aee0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1672640 part 3: Adjust GetNaturalBaselineBOffset implementations to bail (report no baseline) if the frame has 'contain:layout'. r=TYLin, a=RyanVM\n\nSome of our GetNaturalBaselineBOffset implementations already have this; others\ndon't.  But they all should have it, or else a caller might improperly query\ntheir baseline and use it for layout despite the frame having 'contain:layout'.\n\nWithout this patch, the rest of this patch-stack makes us fail WPT test\ncontain-layout-suppress-baseline-002.html because we improperly honor the\nbaseline for the 'contain:layout' buttons at the top of the test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121938", "files": ["layout/forms/nsHTMLButtonControlFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsFlexContainerFrame.h", "layout/generic/nsGridContainerFrame.h", "layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9e7a70ee06f00cc38a98670f619e24575676c69f", "parents": ["c4b852a855cf50a991b30c22405c4ed0f891badf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harry Twyford \u003chtwyford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721585 - Show tooltip for both reader-mode-button and reader-mode-button-icon. r=jaws, a=RyanVM\n\nThe bug was that the tooltip was only being shown for reader-mode-button-icon. The tooltip would show if you hovered right over the icon, and it would be undefined otherwise. This patch shows the tooltip regardless of the hover target. The other items on nodeToTooltipMap and nodeToShortcutMap are toolbarbuttons, so their icons are added in CSS and event handling always sees the parent node as the hover target. The reader mode button icon, however, is an \u003cimage\u003e child of its parent. Either it or its parent could be hover targets. I considered added some handling in GetDynamicShortcutTooltipText along the lines of checking node.closest(reader-mode-button). I settled on just adding more entries to nodeToTooltipMap and nodeToShortcutMap since it's safer and easier to uplift.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122126", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cdf0b19f2bbe258a685c953e6f570cf182cfb3cf", "parents": ["9e7a70ee06f00cc38a98670f619e24575676c69f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1718766, only use session history in parent to get items for back-forward button context menu if items are available, r=Gijs a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122039", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/base/content/test/backforward/browser_history_menu.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8da73f15f7e85dff47e7f6fc1d3992da109b8026", "parents": ["cdf0b19f2bbe258a685c953e6f570cf182cfb3cf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628713013, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "23": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kris Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723321 - Add temporary TSan suppression. r=decoder,mccr8 a=test-only\n\nThis commit also adds a newline to the entry directly above the new suppression, since it was missing one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121545", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2a3ad7cd0a9d6eead7f20355d66ca2ececde18d8", "parents": ["8da73f15f7e85dff47e7f6fc1d3992da109b8026"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723142 - Add temporary TSan suppression. r=decoder,mccr8 a=test-only\n\nThis call appears in the top frames of 2 different stacks (Bug 1723351 and Bug 1723142) so from my understanding it will suppress both test fails. I included both bug numbers for reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121546", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c7a871c2f96be680ff76b96952140f0de195d7c8", "parents": ["2a3ad7cd0a9d6eead7f20355d66ca2ececde18d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723170 - Add temporary TSan suppression. r=decoder,mccr8 a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121548", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a7a9caef0cdb35fb0bcf0064243bbc31ffeb97f9", "parents": ["c7a871c2f96be680ff76b96952140f0de195d7c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723176 - Add temporary TSan suppression. r=decoder,mccr8 a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121549", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e2a7ce600d0259f12e82ce8ff1d9aa6b0a196b23", "parents": ["a7a9caef0cdb35fb0bcf0064243bbc31ffeb97f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Wright \u003ckwright@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723730 - Add temporary TSan suppression. r=mccr8,decoder a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121664", "files": ["mozglue/build/TsanOptions.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4573f7853a1d4a6eda56a8ce998a84cdaa843700", "parents": ["e2a7ce600d0259f12e82ce8ff1d9aa6b0a196b23"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628716628, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "24": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122457", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cbe6965eaee529c0df007b123249630eece20c23", "parents": ["4573f7853a1d4a6eda56a8ce998a84cdaa843700"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628773481, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "jcristau@mozilla.com"}, "25": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1710123 - [devtools] Fix browser_accessibility_reload.js intermittent. r=bomsy, a=test-only\n\nThe test wasn't waiting for the panel to be properly reloaded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122363", "files": ["devtools/client/accessibility/test/browser/browser_accessibility_reload.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "226c75d874f26b14f4014ab9a7f8c971c159cef7", "parents": ["cbe6965eaee529c0df007b123249630eece20c23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1704404 - Apply an explicit line-height to tab labels, in case the title uses fallback fonts with excessive ascent/descent metrics. r=jaws, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120226", "files": ["browser/base/content/tabbrowser.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1741ef6d058fff14a7bf3cf33e54c221ffdd5c83", "parents": ["226c75d874f26b14f4014ab9a7f8c971c159cef7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Goegge \u003cngogge@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722044: Consider loads from external applications as user triggered. r=ckerschb,annevk a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120963", "files": ["dom/security/SecFetch.cpp", "dom/security/test/sec-fetch/browser.ini", "dom/security/test/sec-fetch/browser_external_loads.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "85afb07e80ae3915df697c6696992f48e442c770", "parents": ["1741ef6d058fff14a7bf3cf33e54c221ffdd5c83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1714290 - Don't flush in XULTreeGridAccessible. r=Jamie, a=jcristau\n\nIf comment 5 is right, I don't think that this should be needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121711", "files": ["accessible/xul/XULTreeGridAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b30ed374c4d030430554bab6e1239db59ed90b90", "parents": ["85afb07e80ae3915df697c6696992f48e442c770"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Goegge \u003cngogge@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722703: Consider requests from extension with access to the requested site as Sec-Fetch-Site: 'same-origin'. r=ckerschb,robwu a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121600", "files": ["dom/security/SecFetch.cpp", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_secfetch.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4defecbe7eb83260871dd61ceb567f383d3c661f", "parents": ["b30ed374c4d030430554bab6e1239db59ed90b90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724395, bookmarks commands to add bookmarks and folders not working after a submenu is opened, r=mak a=RyanVM\n\nShould only clear the last trigger node when the top-level popup is hidden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122007", "files": ["browser/components/places/PlacesUIUtils.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8b2055d58e1ee2510d9bf7bbdc4338e1130159d0", "parents": ["4defecbe7eb83260871dd61ceb567f383d3c661f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1701027. Disable partial display list updates when the root scroll frame is modified.  r=mattwoodrow a=RyanVM\n\nThis is basically equivalent to marking the viewport frame modified when the root scroll frame is marked modified.\n\nWe wrap the top layer items in a display wrap list that uses the viewport frame as it's mFrame here\n\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/bb37e6fe8bbe383a57a4ad21a201e26416613ca1/layout/generic/ViewportFrame.cpp#236\n\nSo when we invalidate the root scroll frame for getting a new display port we do a partial update. The wrap list item for the top layer items has a new display item parent, a display async zoom item (the creation of the display port changed this), so the a new display wrap list item is created. All of it's children are matched with the old children of the old display wrap list so those go away, but the old display wrap list item itself sticks around: it's mFrame is the viewport frame which was not marked modified. So the next paint we have these two identical display wrap list items (one empty), and we hit the assert.\n\nSo it seems like we need to mark the viewport frame modified if the root scroll frame is marked modified if we have top layer items (since those top layers items end up being inside the root scroll frames display list). This in turn would disable a partial update for the next paint because ShouldBuildPartial would return false because a viewport frame is modified\n\nhttps://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/bb37e6fe8bbe383a57a4ad21a201e26416613ca1/layout/painting/RetainedDisplayListBuilder.cpp#1309\n\nI'm not sure this is even a bad thing, since we also disable partial updates if the canvas frame (child of the root scroll frame) is marked modified. Perhaps we would want to disable partial updates if the root scroll frame is marked modified, but we can't detect root scroll frames purely from their layout frame type.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D109848", "files": ["layout/painting/RetainedDisplayListBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8a3d467515444f552ec29cda5dc4a578c56977a8", "parents": ["8b2055d58e1ee2510d9bf7bbdc4338e1130159d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1701027. Add test. r=hiro a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120437", "files": ["layout/base/tests/browser.ini", "layout/base/tests/browser_bug1701027-1.js", "layout/base/tests/browser_bug1701027-2.js", "layout/base/tests/helper_bug1701027-1.html", "layout/base/tests/helper_bug1701027-2.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dcf4447a3313074c22118d1f09792b69ed6a699e", "parents": ["8a3d467515444f552ec29cda5dc4a578c56977a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1671525 - Set explicit line-height on urlbarView-row-inner items so that stray characters from math fonts don't result in huge height. r=dao, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120239", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbarView.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3f1a566d56c08055623733614d1dbfe033c8df6", "parents": ["dcf4447a3313074c22118d1f09792b69ed6a699e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722666 - Adjust the urlbar line-height fix from bug 1671525 to avoid potentially clipping glyph descenders. r=dao, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121188", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbarView.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "06ca0328897868256c8c03ab8928b16be6cb9fe9", "parents": ["e3f1a566d56c08055623733614d1dbfe033c8df6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628797117, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "26": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721437 - Render clear tiles before alpha tiles. r=bradwerth, a=RyanVM\n\nBefore this patch the clear tiles were drawn last which meant they would always be drawn on top of all transparent content. It was finde under the assumption that nothing is ever rendered on top of clear tiles, however it turns out to be an issue with the proton window modal darkining which renders some semi-transparent black on top of the whole window (including window controls on windows 8 which use clear tiles). Since the occlusion culling treats clear tiles as opaque they will cut through anything under them regardless of the drawing order, so we can render them before transaprent tiles to get the correct result which is to overwrite what's under the clear tile while still being able to render semi-transparent content on top.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120844", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5a91fcbdf37d613187a059e028635dcd907664d5", "parents": ["06ca0328897868256c8c03ab8928b16be6cb9fe9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722566 - Add null checks in PEHeaders::FindResourceLeaf. r=mhowell, a=RyanVM\n\nWe had crashes in `PEHeaders::FindResourceLeaf` where `idDir` was nullptr.  This can\nhappen when the resource table is modified by a third-party application and an entry\nin the table points to somewhere outside the executable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121093", "files": ["mozglue/misc/NativeNt.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "272617a59467a26ac4033a21d55991b834ba464e", "parents": ["5a91fcbdf37d613187a059e028635dcd907664d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723868 - Skip msvp9dec_store.dll in GetInfoForSelf(). r=gerald, a=RyanVM\n\nWhen mfplat.dll loads msvp9dec_store.dll, it posts a task\nto unload the module to the work queue even if msvp9dec_store.dll\nis already loaded and mfplat.dll skips LoadLibrary.  Therefore,\nwe cannot safely lock msvp9dec_store.dll by loading it as data.\n\nThe proposed fix is to skip processing the module.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121777", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/shared-libraries-win32.cc", "tools/profiler/core/shared-libraries-win32.cc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38acd685ea4cd57e189b63af3b55c21049d46cd2", "parents": ["272617a59467a26ac4033a21d55991b834ba464e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Svelto \u003cgsvelto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723941 - Fix several issues in macOS minidump generation which can lead to hangs & crashes. r=KrisWright, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121725", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad-client/mac/crash_generation/crash_generation_client.cc", "toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad-client/mac/crash_generation/crash_generation_server.cc"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e6ead7489f31347c82461ada7e0618d1652f4d9c", "parents": ["38acd685ea4cd57e189b63af3b55c21049d46cd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1720050 - Ensure to listen to transition events on \u003cselect\u003e, not bubbled events from options. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nOptions can change styles for a variety of reasons and we don't want\ntransitions on them to re-update the whole menulist.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121353", "files": ["toolkit/actors/SelectChild.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8758e4c1ce1d38ffd5aa36e75b489a36e21e617a", "parents": ["e6ead7489f31347c82461ada7e0618d1652f4d9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harry Twyford \u003chtwyford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722395 - Fix placeholder string in handoff input in permanent private browsing mode. r=Standard8, a=RyanVM\n\nabout:newtab doesn't load aboutPrivateBrowsing.ftl and conversely about:privatebrowsing doesn't load newtab.ftl. Since permanent private browsing mode uses about:newtab as its new tab, we need to make sure we load our strings from newtab.ftl in that case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121646", "files": ["browser/actors/ContentSearchParent.jsm", "browser/components/search/content/contentSearchHandoffUI.js", "browser/components/search/content/contentSearchUI.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_contentSearchUI_default.js", "browser/modules/test/browser/browser_ContentSearch.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4c022fcfe47ac14cff31881e3c953189a0879b0e", "parents": ["8758e4c1ce1d38ffd5aa36e75b489a36e21e617a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1663571, r=mak a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D89680", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cf092366a25d781afa10045d0ed9bc030d13631a", "parents": ["4c022fcfe47ac14cff31881e3c953189a0879b0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724107, be more precise when counting the number of allocator users, r=KrisWright a=RyanVM\n\nThe patch is based on code inspection.\n\nOne could move sAllocatorUsers also to Free(), but shouldn't matter in practise.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121868", "files": ["xpcom/threads/TimerThread.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7134058c114c0f8d55981e4c7fd1e3bac65eda2e", "parents": ["cf092366a25d781afa10045d0ed9bc030d13631a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bernard Igiri \u003cbigiri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1710629 - Adjust bookmarks menu button panel padding. r=mak, a=RyanVM\n\nModified bookmarks menu button panel padding in Windows and Linux to match the appearance of that panel in MacOS.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119643", "files": ["browser/themes/osx/customizableui/panelUI.css", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fd34cd0543a4f428424352bac804641bc10492e4", "parents": ["7134058c114c0f8d55981e4c7fd1e3bac65eda2e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1628800047, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "27": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717575 - Check given attributes for null before iterating. r=morgan, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119789", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5a4b54a49fe775df43cdb54e9f8be83b2d5e880b", "parents": ["fd34cd0543a4f428424352bac804641bc10492e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars T Hansen \u003clhansen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723930 - Do not special-case declared-unaligned accesses on ARM. r=jseward, a=RyanVM\n\nSince early on, code generation on ARM has emulated accesses that are\ndeclared as unaligned (the align= attribute has a value that is less\nthan the natural alignment for the datum) by emitting individual byte\naccesses.  There's almost no good reason to continue to do this, as we\nare completely dependent on other mechanisms for handling accesses\nthat are actually unaligned (the effective address does not have\nnatural alignment) though declared to be aligned:\n\n- For integer accesses we are dependent on the hardware/OS to support\n  actually-unaligned accesses transparently.\n\n- For FP accesses we handle signals originating from\n  actually-unaligned accesses that are not handled by hardware/OS, but\n  that code is being rewritten over in bug 1587757 to avoid the trap\n  handling altogether by using unaligned-friendly instructions.\n\n(Some of the code ripped out in this patch comes back in the patch for\nbug 1587757, though in a different form.)\n\nThe only reason to continue using individual byte accesses would be\nperformance: if the CPU does not support unaligned accesses and the OS\nhas to emulate them in a trap handler, programs could be faster by\navoiding the traps.  Yet such hardware is increasingly nonexistent.\nAlso, this solution would depend on the tools to declare accesses as\npotentially-unaligned in all appropriate cases, and that is almost\ncertainly not going to happen.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121832", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/CodeGenerator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/LIR-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm/Lowering-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "77e8cec27de4732610b55007ccdb653e26c04891", "parents": ["5a4b54a49fe775df43cdb54e9f8be83b2d5e880b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars T Hansen \u003clhansen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1587757 - Avoid signal handling for unaligned accesses. r=jseward, a=RyanVM\n\nOn ARM, the VLDR and VSTR instructions can't handle unaligned\naccesses, instead they will generally trap with a SIGBUS.  Some time\nago I added code to handle the trap and emulate the instructions in\nthe trap handler.  This emulation is brittle in the sense that it\ndepends on information about kernel data structures, and that\ninformation is not always available.  So we need to handle this\ndifferently, as follows.\n\nThis patch removes the SIGBUS handling and the load/store emulation,\nand instead uses other instructions than VLDR/VSTR to handle FP loads\nand stores.\n\nOn NEON-equipped systems (on almost all ARMv7 systems and on all ARMv8\nsystems), use the NEON VLD1 and VST1 instructions - they can deal with\nunaligned data just fine.\n\nOn non-NEON-equipped systems, use a fallback path via integer load and\nstore, moving integer data to and from the FP register file.\n\nBoth paths depend on us seeing no unaligned traps, ie, either\nSCTRL.A=0, or the kernel handling alignment traps when SCTRL.A=1.  But\nwe've long since assumed that unaligned integer loads and stores will\nJust Work under exactly those conditions, so this is going to have to\ncount as good enough.  (And it's what V8 did, last I looked.)\n\nAs our assembler, simulator, and disassembler don't currently support\nNEON much at all, I've had to add various support for VLD1/VST1, both\nnew variants and a drive-by fix to an existing VLD1 variant that\ndidn't handle wasm traps.\n\nFor code that does not use unaligned FP accesses, the performance of\nthe new NEON code should be the same as the old code, while the new\nnon-NEON code might be a hair slower (this is OK since almost all\nsystems have NEON).  For code that does use unaligned FP accesses,\nperformance should be much better, as we avoid the signal handler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121833", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm/Architecture-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Architecture-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm/Assembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Assembler-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Simulator-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/disasm/Disasm-arm.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmInstance.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmInstance.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmSignalHandlers.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "234ffd840625cd3b43c54c71aa386cf45c4f80c4", "parents": ["77e8cec27de4732610b55007ccdb653e26c04891"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars T Hansen \u003clhansen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724475 - Handle unaligned loads to high singles differently. r=jseward, a=RyanVM\n\nWhen the target register of an unaligned FP load is the high single\nof a pair, we must go via a temp.  The reason is that the architecture\nforbids unaligned loads to target the high single.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122112", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm/Assembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Simulator-arm.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8977bf49f426b9c3d70c84132c3f3649a5363707", "parents": ["234ffd840625cd3b43c54c71aa386cf45c4f80c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724675 - Ensure Synced Tabs panel CtA button label is visible. r=mhowell, a=RyanVM\n\nIn bug 1698883, a more general rule was removed that made the label for\nthe Synced Tabs panel CtA button visible: https://hg.mozilla.org/integration/autoland/rev/0ff3ea52f07954501fbcfe9e6abe2a62cfb37d9b#l7.13\n\nSince that rule isn't around anymore, we tell the Synced Tabs button\nexplicitly to display itself. Thankfully, we no longer need to override\nthe text-align property with !important, since that was in the original\nrule that was removed, and the text-shadow is already being set to none\nin another rule for this button.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122371", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "977e4b88de0532cfdf017a962681885f25801b86", "parents": ["8977bf49f426b9c3d70c84132c3f3649a5363707"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724101 - Protect nsHtml5StreamListener::mDelegate with a monitor. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122471", "files": ["parser/html/moz.build", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamListener.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamListener.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParser.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParserPtr.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParserReleaser.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3528c25674112da76558a342e06e14849bce58c5", "parents": ["977e4b88de0532cfdf017a962681885f25801b86"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629044126, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "28": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "No bug - bump version to 91.0.1. a=release", "files": ["browser/config/version.txt", "browser/config/version_display.txt", "config/milestone.txt"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3fba336ac5dac88f1c19b87e51320925e4699e92", "parents": ["42e1acb39affae65d50ced864d28672d67aa0181"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-release repo-update remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121836", "files": ["services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ae16d3dd5b359f783763289783c89b6f9270ccf8", "parents": ["3fba336ac5dac88f1c19b87e51320925e4699e92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-release repo-update remote-settings - a=repo-update, r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122067", "files": ["services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/onecrl.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aa43942c342705dac7bf74b7e9654edc808293c5", "parents": ["ae16d3dd5b359f783763289783c89b6f9270ccf8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-release repo-update remote-settings - a=repo-update r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122698", "files": ["services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "15c753e2630d6014833b3917789d9d814878a3ab", "parents": ["aa43942c342705dac7bf74b7e9654edc808293c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dragana Damjanovic \u003cdd.mozilla@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1724896 - Sanitize headers. r=necko-reviewers,valentin, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122294", "files": ["netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4f3e0758a0ced30fa1cf4a4577f74aa71770aae7", "parents": ["15c753e2630d6014833b3917789d9d814878a3ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1704404 - Apply an explicit line-height to tab labels, in case the title uses fallback fonts with excessive ascent/descent metrics. r=jaws, a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120226", "files": ["browser/base/content/tabbrowser.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b5dd294ee5058f0ac8b3fa5c5cb236d6c5d5f762", "parents": ["4f3e0758a0ced30fa1cf4a4577f74aa71770aae7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jeff Muizelaar \u003cjmuizelaar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1721903 - Add the error code when we fail to Map a tile. a=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120675", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorD3D11SWGL.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9bc887edd6ad40d577ba23cc57494a814ef2d287", "parents": ["b5dd294ee5058f0ac8b3fa5c5cb236d6c5d5f762"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "FIREFOX_ESR_91_0_X_RELBRANCH", "desc": "Bug 1718329 - Gracefully handle device reset when mapping tiles with SW-WR + D3D11 compositing. r=jrmuizel, a=jcristau\n\nIf we encounter a device reset in\nRenderCompositorD3D11SWGL::TileD3D11::Map, we should fail the call, and\nrely upon the device reset checks at the end of a render pass to\nrecreate our compositor sessions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121251", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorD3D11SWGL.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null]