"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1714583 - allow nsIFile::Create to skip creating ancestor directories, to fix IOUtils::makeDirectory, to fix UNC default download folders, r=barret,xpcom-reviewers,mccr8 a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120338", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/system/IOUtils.cpp", "dom/system/tests/ioutils/test_ioutils_mkdir.html", "xpcom/io/FileDescriptorFile.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsIFile.idl", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileUnix.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileUnix.h", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e3a57c25bbdf837c4d0403e3e7eaba4d14688e88", "parents": ["cab57ff2ff7b48dc2f61a03b87b3476ba6eb071e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721665 - Do not overwrite private browsing permission lifetime when removing permissions. r=timhuang, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121749", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/browser.ini", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_permissions_dialog_default_perm.js", "extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "95004c624bbf9651205a3157c8ff35c5d9e13dc2", "parents": ["e3a57c25bbdf837c4d0403e3e7eaba4d14688e88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721084 - Do not clear auth tokens and auth cache when purging trackers. r=johannh, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122864", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/PurgeTrackerService.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "64906fa7e47ea49a9678056088a876486d20e0b2", "parents": ["95004c624bbf9651205a3157c8ff35c5d9e13dc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1715965 - Handle errors for local XPIs installed by policy. r=mixedpuppy, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D120763", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_addon_update.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_extensionsettings.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dc8b55a1466bce1a644248c722be3e805ad72e82", "parents": ["64906fa7e47ea49a9678056088a876486d20e0b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Miko Mynttinen \u003cmikokm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1719346 - Do not cache borders. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121000", "files": ["layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/reftests/display-list/1719346-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/display-list/1719346-1.gif", "layout/reftests/display-list/1719346-1.html", "layout/reftests/display-list/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1b7b0de08d4c74729ab973e90c4a7d8a0263468e", "parents": ["dc8b55a1466bce1a644248c722be3e805ad72e82"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629399864, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "35": {"changesets": [{"author": "Toshihito Kikuchi \u003ctkikuchi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1711126 - The module index in the third-party modules ping may be -1. r=mhowell, a=test-only\n\nThis patch updates the regex pattern to match data where the module index of\na callstack is -1 or a non-negative integer.  -1 is legitimately set in\n`CreateJSStackObject` when the frame address is not within any module in the\nmodule list.\n\nIf the pattern did not match in debug build, calling `toBoolean()` hit the\nassert because `matchResult` was not a boolean but null.  This patch fixes\nthat problem, too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122020", "files": ["toolkit/xre/test/gtest/TestUntrustedModules.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0531d1d4b562552ec660a21a6ce6e0bd89df29bb", "parents": ["1b7b0de08d4c74729ab973e90c4a7d8a0263468e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1720877 - ensure we do not offer reader mode for PDFs by checking base URI as well as document URI when checking for reader-ability, r=robwu a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122960", "files": ["browser/actors/AboutReaderChild.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a4ae77fad8e9191034e890064a756355a8d84c4c", "parents": ["0531d1d4b562552ec660a21a6ce6e0bd89df29bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725223 - Reset native styles of #UITourHighlightContainer properly. r=dao, a=RyanVM\n\nThis is needed for macOS / windows because of this rule:\n\n  https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/36904ac58d2528fc59f640db57cc9429103368d3/toolkit/themes/osx/global/popup.css#12-15\n\nThis should be a better fix than double-applying the background.\n\nLonger term it might be worth trying to make panels `appearance: none` (and no\nbackground / borders on the panel itself, only on the contents) by default, and\nadd a `native` attribute or such for the ones that should look native, wdyt?\n\nI can look into that if it'd be useful.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122583", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/UITour.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "23ab9c2a54db90ef293eeffe628e64f30b48373e", "parents": ["a4ae77fad8e9191034e890064a756355a8d84c4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722662 - Make Element::{Add,Remove}States handle change notifications correctly. r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nThe style system uses the changed bits to compute the old state, so if\nit's inaccurate it might cause styles to be incorrectly invalidated.\n\nThis causes issues because with the next patch the autofill jsm\ncalls removeManuallyManagedStates(AUTOFILL), then\naddManuallyManagedStates(AUTOFILL | AUTOFILL_PREVIEW), and if the input\ndidn't have AUTOFILL before we'd incorrectly detect it as not changing\nwith the next patch.\n\nAlso make them not virtual anymore since nobody overrides them. An\nalternative to this would be to assert that we don't yet have the state\nwe're adding (or that we have the state we're removing), and handle it\nin the callers. But this is a bit more convenient.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122013", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Element.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ae0d7cd33780e237f7d15f7dda79705163bda0bb", "parents": ["23ab9c2a54db90ef293eeffe628e64f30b48373e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722662 - Make :-moz-autofill-preview imply :autofill. r=hiro, a=RyanVM\n\nThis is useful so that author rules for :autofill also work for the\nautofill preview.\n\nIt also makes the UA sheet in forms.css simpler (otherwise we'd need to\ntweak the selectors to put :-moz-autofill-preview everywhere we put\n:autofill).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122014", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillHandler.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9f615f29203bbf6fe8fae0e89cb3a7fc0a43e77f", "parents": ["ae0d7cd33780e237f7d15f7dda79705163bda0bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722662 - Load SpecialPowers in reftests. r=jgraham,jmaher a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D122014\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122015", "files": ["layout/tools/reftest/reftestcommandline.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e2d127e96624acb59fcfb6b8dddaacc96cfb7c2e", "parents": ["9f615f29203bbf6fe8fae0e89cb3a7fc0a43e77f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722662 - Add tests for autofill rendering. r=hiro, a=RyanVM\n\nThey're not the prettiest, but that's all that needs to happen right now for\nautofill to work.\n\nDepends on D122015\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122016", "files": ["layout/reftests/forms/input/text/autofill-blank.html", "layout/reftests/forms/input/text/autofill-preview-blank.html", "layout/reftests/forms/input/text/autofill-preview.html", "layout/reftests/forms/input/text/autofill.html", "layout/reftests/forms/input/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bb7bcecb1f93768e487924fd30d6bb41f07da9e0", "parents": ["e2d127e96624acb59fcfb6b8dddaacc96cfb7c2e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629487903, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "36": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723787 - Apply cairo quartz font/surface changes from Andrea Canciani's quartz-colored-glyphs branch at https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/ranma42/cairo/-/commits/quartz-colored-glyphs. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121909", "files": ["gfx/cairo/cairo/src/cairo-quartz-font.c", "gfx/cairo/cairo/src/cairo-quartz-private.h", "gfx/cairo/cairo/src/cairo-quartz-surface.c"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e965e3865d4a034ed5dbb2d3ca988e5bb3b5aa75", "parents": ["bb7bcecb1f93768e487924fd30d6bb41f07da9e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723787 - Add print reftest to verify that emoji are not blank when printing. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121948", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/emoji-print.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e5b6d72b8ff5397e84a0649b8b70d4f67f3df8cd", "parents": ["e965e3865d4a034ed5dbb2d3ca988e5bb3b5aa75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos Alvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724120 - Tweak Windows' nsWindow::SetCursor. r=mhowell, a=RyanVM\n\nThis is simpler and more correct, the previous code could get sHCursor and\nsCurrentCursor out of sync, which caused this issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122966", "files": ["widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "49557cbee449eb7e5bd34e2f86f1f7da0a23c82d", "parents": ["e5b6d72b8ff5397e84a0649b8b70d4f67f3df8cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1721107 - block mk protocol, r=dveditz, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123214", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "452e0a21940d512ce68527dc2446d7c1fbfe4dba", "parents": ["49557cbee449eb7e5bd34e2f86f1f7da0a23c82d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629648654, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "37": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123323", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aeb8371de862b9b24328edcc10f0e9c1ee496242", "parents": ["452e0a21940d512ce68527dc2446d7c1fbfe4dba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1715291 - Fix text in \u003cinput\u003e is clipped by inline-end padding. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nThe fix in Bug 1696885 is not correct when the width of the text in\n\u003cinput\u003e is shorter than the width of the \u003cinput\u003e, but is long enough to\nbe covered by its inline-end padding.\n\nThis patch's idea is similar to the old code [1] before applying bug\n1696885, but only tweak the scrollable overflow area in the inline axis.\n\n[1] https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/c3ee9188d2f9020764db9daf8fa47a07fa3311c9/layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp#785-806\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123244", "files": ["layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-input-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-input-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-input-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollable-overflow-input-002.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "3cef3c2717b65231dfde22eafd06a22830cbfe2e", "parents": ["aeb8371de862b9b24328edcc10f0e9c1ee496242"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1726515 - Workaround GCC-calling-into-LLVM ABI issue by making GenericFontFamily larger. r=hiro, a=RyanVM\n\nThis enum being a bit larger doesn't cause many common data structures\nto grow, so this should be fine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123146", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxTypes.h", "servo/components/style/values/computed/font.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "65fd2287abed757b334ee446da677d5664182ae9", "parents": ["3cef3c2717b65231dfde22eafd06a22830cbfe2e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1704110 - Added PreflightCacheCleaner. r=necko-reviewers,johannh,dragana a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119290", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsCORSListenerProxy.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsCORSListenerProxy.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsIHttpProtocolHandler.idl", "toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.jsm", "toolkit/components/cleardata/nsIClearDataService.idl", "toolkit/components/cleardata/tests/browser/browser.ini", "toolkit/components/cleardata/tests/browser/browser_preflight_cache.js", "toolkit/components/cleardata/tests/browser/file_cors_preflight.sjs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f720fe89d32e2ffc849d92015a5bb3fc1e3a2c7e", "parents": ["65fd2287abed757b334ee446da677d5664182ae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Zuehlcke \u003cpbz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1727146 - Only clear the preflight cache on user request. r=johannh, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123134", "files": ["toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.jsm", "toolkit/components/cleardata/tests/browser/browser_preflight_cache.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "125ff13575ea3e8f8f4c65dff709ceca533d2a87", "parents": ["f720fe89d32e2ffc849d92015a5bb3fc1e3a2c7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Lemley \u003crob@thunderbird.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1726216 - Fix thunderbird91-next regex in update_verify_config.py. r=jmaher, a=RyanVM\n\nThe missing closing single quote causes update-verify-config-next to fail as\nthe value is used in a shell commandline.\nAdded a quick test to look for this kind of error since apparently it is easy\nto miss.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122901", "files": ["taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/update_verify_config.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "71156356c6825a988109545c72a79df597c6da6d", "parents": ["125ff13575ea3e8f8f4c65dff709ceca533d2a87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724777, optimize suppressed MicroTask handling, r=mccr8 a=RyanVM\n\nThe test is in theory racy, but trying to limit the cases when it might behave badly\nby running it on opt desktop builds only. Without the patch the 'period' check takes over 400ms locally and with the\npatch 1-3ms.\n\nThe changes are just trying to optimize execution, not change the behavior.\nUse of SuppressedMicroTasks is perhaps a bit odd, but it helps keeping\nSavedMicroTaskQueue and similar code simple.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122290", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/base/test/test_suppressed_microtasks.html", "dom/workers/RuntimeService.cpp", "dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.cpp", "dom/worklet/WorkletThread.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "877d9fcafe671bdabf817a1eaeda4dc2bd7b9d73", "parents": ["71156356c6825a988109545c72a79df597c6da6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724899, suppress microtasks and timers only in the current tab when dom.input_events.canSuspendInBCG.enabled is false, r=kashav a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D122290\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122298", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/test/test_suppressed_microtasks.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "90a4f159845364a5ee5734080801e931d6be1806", "parents": ["877d9fcafe671bdabf817a1eaeda4dc2bd7b9d73"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629840923, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "38": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1715603 - part 1: Don't extend selection into a link. r=edgar, a=RyanVM\n\nIf middle button click with `Shift` key occurs, Chrome and Safari extend the\nselection in most cases.  However, if the clicked position is in a link,\nChrome does:\n* If editable, collapse selection into the link instead of extending selection.\n* If not editable, not extending selection and open tabs.\n\nWe should follow this behavior for both backward compatibility and web-compat.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119252", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/test/test_selection_changes_with_middle_mouse_button.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/selection/contenteditable/modifying-selection-with-primary-mouse-button.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/selection/contenteditable/modifying-selection-with-middle-mouse-button.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/selection/contenteditable/modifying-selection-with-primary-mouse-button.tentative.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "39537a4196d4102c160f39b7286e64bbfeafbe4e", "parents": ["90a4f159845364a5ee5734080801e931d6be1806"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1715603 - part 2: Make `AutoScrollChild` not start autoscroll if a modifier key is pressed. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nNow, `nsIFrame::HandleEvent` moves selection at middle mouse button down.  This\noccurs before dispatching the event into the system event group.  Therefore,\n`AutoScrollChild` cannot prevent it.\n\nOn the other hand, Chrome does not start autoscroll when a modifier is pressed.\nThis means that our users may not be able to use middle click with modifiers\nif web apps do not call `preventDefault()` as expected.  So, this difference\nis a potential risk of web-compat.\n\nTherefore, this patch makes `AutoScrollChild` stop starting autoscroll if\n`Shift` key is pressed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D119253", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/actors/AutoScrollChild.jsm", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_click_event_during_autoscrolling.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "48135b8a330e61f8310297c20963e54dd8b8b5b8", "parents": ["39537a4196d4102c160f39b7286e64bbfeafbe4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi Lee \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1717603 - Ensure FormAutofill loads its script on all the opened window. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nThis patch uses Services.wm.getEnumerator(\"\") instead of Services.wm.getEnumerator(\"navigator:browser\")\nto ensure we get all the opened window during FormAutofill initialization. See WindowTrackerBase#*browserWindows\nin ext-tabs-base.js for more details.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121364", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fe6e71bec6aa78a50f9121c5cc6176904fdcfa5e", "parents": ["48135b8a330e61f8310297c20963e54dd8b8b5b8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629848390, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "39": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1723920 - Ensure aPrivateBrowsingId input is proper. r=janv, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122578", "files": ["dom/storage/StorageCommon.h", "dom/storage/StorageDBThread.cpp", "dom/storage/StorageIPC.cpp", "dom/storage/StorageObserver.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9fc43bd3dfe1d31c672254ccb4fb536a0a87f47c", "parents": ["fe6e71bec6aa78a50f9121c5cc6176904fdcfa5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722535 - Make `HTMLEditor` call `HTMLEditUtils::GetBetterInsertionPoint()` with an editing host which is not limited in the `\u003cbody\u003e` r=m_kato a=RyanVM\n\nPreviously, `HTMLEditor::GetBetterInsertionPoint()` didn't check whether\ngiven point is in an editing host or not.  However, now\n`HTMLEditUtils::GetBetterInsertionPoint()` does it with editing host which\nis returned by `HTMLEditor::GetActiveEditingHost(LimitInBodyElement::No)`.\nHowever, the old behavior is exactly same as\n`HTMLEditor::GetActiveEditingHost(LimitInBodyElement::Yes)` if editing host\nis outside the `\u003cbody\u003e` element.\n\nFor taking back the original behavior, we should call the method with the\nresult of the latter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121370", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.ini", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_pasting_in_temporarily_created_div_outside_body.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9ad996eae2c57b210de3d6130d5264e3cd3de883", "parents": ["9fc43bd3dfe1d31c672254ccb4fb536a0a87f47c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722535 - Add WPT to test basic edit commands in `\u003cdiv\u003e` element outside `\u003cbody\u003e` element r=m_kato a=RyanVM\n\nDepends on D121370\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121371", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/editing/other/editing-div-outside-body.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/editing-div-outside-body.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "edf5e6f83035ecb93f4d84060acd2a2c25e9c697", "parents": ["9ad996eae2c57b210de3d6130d5264e3cd3de883"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars T Hansen \u003clhansen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1720650 - Fix codegen problem in narrowing. r=yury, a=RyanVM\n\nThe ARM64 architecture uses two instructions to implement SIMD narrowing,\nSQXTN and SQXTN2 (and their unsigned-saturation variants).  These are not\nquite symmetric: the former will clear the upper bits of the output register\nand set the lower bits, while the latter will just set the upper bits.\nTo implement an across-the-vector narrowing, the former must be executed\nbefore the latter.\n\nFor some operations, we execute them in the other order to save a move.\nBut this is incorrect, so this patch reintroduces the move when it\nis required.  This effectively makes the three-address operations the\nsame as the two-address operations and it's possible we want to\npropagate the fix higher up in the stack to avoid the duplication of\ncode, but for now a local fix seems best.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122587", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64-inl.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "13973594eb37054c35a326defd41820d32c6e1c2", "parents": ["edf5e6f83035ecb93f4d84060acd2a2c25e9c697"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725638. r=lth, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123101", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/MoveEmitter-arm64.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6a6f716a03ba20f04f468dea195bc615f00fc60b", "parents": ["13973594eb37054c35a326defd41820d32c6e1c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1726606: Default browser.display.document_color_use to 1 on MacOS. r=emilio, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123142", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/telemetry/browser_HCM_telemetry.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9e69a6210f885d2931fa98af4bd50e422d276af4", "parents": ["6a6f716a03ba20f04f468dea195bc615f00fc60b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629917884, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "40": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emma Malysz \u003cemalysz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724194: ensure close button is visible in findbar. r=jaws, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123392", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser.inc.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/findbar.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/findbar.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "37ea3067e3894702a2b46ad19313279c2068ba7a", "parents": ["9e69a6210f885d2931fa98af4bd50e422d276af4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harry Twyford \u003chtwyford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725146 - Force ColorScheme::Light in NativeGetColor on macOS \u003c 10.14. r=mstange, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D122766", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsLookAndFeel.mm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "b2a5a197e0a17db012f095f6de80015b438214c6", "parents": ["37ea3067e3894702a2b46ad19313279c2068ba7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Molly Howell \u003cmhowell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1705684 - Correct download details panel spacing. r=dao, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123401", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/downloads/downloads.inc.css"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "62db48218c72356ca9d2097838ebb353b7d9eb32", "parents": ["b2a5a197e0a17db012f095f6de80015b438214c6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629930742, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "41": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722136 - [devtools] Wait for a valid presShell in devtools/client/shared tests r=nchevobbe a=test-only DONTBUILD\n\nFor context, see the bug conversation. We have a class of issues on popup related tests on linux webrender.\nI suspect they are triggered because we don't have a presShell yet when we try to create popups.\nThis patch adds a waitForPresShell helper in shared-head, and uses it from the createHost test helper, which is used by most of the failing tests, as well as from a specific test: browser_enable_devtools_popup_new_user.js\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121798", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/test/browser_enable_devtools_popup_new_user.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/head.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/shared-head.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ba100ac145a044bf97f757065f507e1f96bbee11", "parents": ["62db48218c72356ca9d2097838ebb353b7d9eb32"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629978761, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "42": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722725 - Fix benign race in AsyncPanZoomController::SetTestAsyncScrollOffset. r=gfx-reviewers,jrmuizel, a=jcristau\n\nThis got tripped in the tsan tests, but should only happen during\ntesting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121092", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "f95218665b85d3a9426cbf2c668ea74ce8ed40a3", "parents": ["ba100ac145a044bf97f757065f507e1f96bbee11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123744", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c6fa379b39f65d9c9b68a566ebf62e44c7eefe6f", "parents": ["f95218665b85d3a9426cbf2c668ea74ce8ed40a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725416 - Default to eNotPressed in WidgetTouchEvent. r=edgar, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123100", "files": ["dom/events/test/pointerevents/mochitest.ini", "dom/events/test/pointerevents/test_bug1725416.html", "widget/InputData.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ecd759a45b3dd57979eac66914b9d660f70f2399", "parents": ["c6fa379b39f65d9c9b68a566ebf62e44c7eefe6f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1629982801, "git_changesets": [null, null, null], "user": "jcristau@mozilla.com"}, "43": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123929", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/search-config.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8911928e4cacc83a4984f2bbfa573b4fbc2325d7", "parents": ["ecd759a45b3dd57979eac66914b9d660f70f2399"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1725032 - Override transparent Window system color on 10.13 with a light gray. r=harry, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123631", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsLookAndFeel.mm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "33d412ef4fc145a5806a5d5f7be56a935833da6f", "parents": ["8911928e4cacc83a4984f2bbfa573b4fbc2325d7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1630349177, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "44": {"changesets": [{"author": "Neil Deakin \u003cneil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1694941, wait for sound to start playing before treating a sound-playing tab as ready, r=mconley a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123746", "files": ["browser/modules/test/browser/browser_TabUnloader.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "332e07f2c0b32d037a6f5818077731b37bb0e5df", "parents": ["33d412ef4fc145a5806a5d5f7be56a935833da6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1678352 - Don't GoFaster in AudioInputTrackDisabling. r=pehrsons, a=test-only\n\nIn retrospect this is too dependent on scheduling. We can and should do\nsomething better. This will be easier to implement once I implement real offline\nsupport for suspend/resume for offline MediaTrackGraph for OfflineAudioContext I\nthink.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123730", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1f10d0160e5aa1b629bf0837cf3ee31ba35856c7", "parents": ["332e07f2c0b32d037a6f5818077731b37bb0e5df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Hirsch \u003cjhirsch@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1724081 - Stop sending analytics pings to the Screenshots server. r=emalysz, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121796", "files": ["browser/extensions/screenshots/background/analytics.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "769b135ba3ffbc3565a17ee9caf79e6817219452", "parents": ["1f10d0160e5aa1b629bf0837cf3ee31ba35856c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1718796 - Use DocShell to get last transaction id of root PresContext; r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D123464", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d015edeaf1a75b6bd672f9f9a413251482b715d6", "parents": ["769b135ba3ffbc3565a17ee9caf79e6817219452"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_91_1_0esr_BUILD1", "FIREFOX_91_1_0esr_RELEASE"]}], "date": 1630500918, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}}
}";